items.evaluationCriteria:
The evidence list is pre-defined, but no pass/fail thresholds exist. Design §9 "New measurements (these decide approval)" lists 7 required measurements:
1. stepwise attribution per position;
2. anchor-setter audit;
3. population sizes;
4. both consumer populations;
5. day/week stability under real status churn;
6. consumer effect with #1890's flag fixed OFF/ON;
7. latency and cache behaviour.
It also requires a production-box replay before approval. The owner record says "Provide measured before-and-after evidence before requesting activation."
Engineering gates for P3 (design §6/§8): flag-off byte identity, per-consumer parity, a replay stepwise table.
Numeric acceptance thresholds for activation: NONE_DEFINED. This is a blocker for any activation decision; recommend the owner preregister acceptance criteria in the P4 evidence package, for example which anchor or consumer-effect magnitudes are acceptable.

